{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the goal to maximize the total value of Carelland's exports (i.e., the value of domestically produced steel, engines, electronics, and plastic sold on the world market), or is it to maximize the net value after subtracting the cost of the Klunz imported goods used in production?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single binary choice regarding the objective function (gross export value vs. net value), which constitutes one semantically independent clarification question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say maximize domestic GDP, do you mean the total value of all four domestically produced goods (steel, engines, electronics, plastic) at their world-market prices, or the value of domestic production minus the value of the Klunz imported goods used as inputs?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy definition choice between two mutually exclusive interpretations of 'maximize domestic GDP'."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "To pin down the objective, is the quantity to maximize the total value of the four domestically produced goods (steel, engines, electronics, plastic) at their world-market prices, with the Klunz imported goods treated as a free input that does not reduce the objective?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single compound clarification question asking for confirmation of the objective function definition, including how imported goods are treated. Since it asks for a single policy/definition choice, it counts as one atomic question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the quantities of steel, engines, electronics, and plastic that Carelland produces all available for export at the given world-market prices, or is some of the production consumed domestically as an input to other production (e.g., the 0.8 steel used per engine) and therefore not counted in the export value?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy choice regarding how production quantities are treated in the export calculation (fully exportable vs. partially consumed domestically)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are these inputs consumed from Carelland's own domestic production of those goods, meaning domestic production of steel must cover both the steel exported and the steel used as input in making engines, electronics, and plastic?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of a specific accounting assumption regarding input consumption sources."
}

